#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:3
#: 4258cbfa86f44a37ac38d4c815d4c70e
msgid "How to set up a test bench"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:6
#: 2dbbb679e3ad4b2fa429066c4d4ff2df
msgid ""
"This guide shows how to set up simple test bench that automatically test "
"your code you’re about to push. It is written especially for ``core3`` "
"branch of ``core-admin.git`` repo, but some ideas are universal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:8
#: cb16433822a648c59fe0cbd39e0c7bc3
msgid ""
"We will set up a spare machine (bare metal, not a virtual) that will be "
"hosting our experimental Dom0. We will communicate with it via Ethernet and "
"SSH. This tutorial assumes you are familiar with :doc:`QubesBuilder </"
"developer/building/qubes-builder>` and you have it set up and running "
"flawlessly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:10
#: ee04ecd7ad1f402cb305f064dbf9c2ca
msgid ""
"**Notice:** This setup intentionally weakens some security properties in the "
"testing system. So make sure you understand the risks and use exclusively "
"for testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:13
#: e38512ebc58c428ca28dfe8c40337732
msgid "Setting up the Machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:17
#: 5f5e9f8d23c440b4af4eb85c21355a22
msgid "Install ISO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:20
#: ac1670602e9f41f5906784000ca36490
msgid ""
"First, do a clean install from the ``.iso`` :doc:`you built </developer/"
"building/qubes-iso-building>` or grabbed elsewhere (for example `here "
"<https://forum.qubes-os.org/t/qubesos-4-1-alpha-signed-weekly-"
"builds/3601>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:23
#: 1c8b1a01f4794161bbc45169da332f29
msgid "Enabling Network Access in Dom0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:26
#: 43650d8dd972400d87c80927cb028bd8
msgid ""
"Internet access is intentionally disabled by default in dom0. But to ease "
"the deployment process we will give it access. The following steps should be "
"done in ``dom0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:28
#: 2d3f234f63e74190976b6cfa599d1fd9
msgid ""
"**Note:** the following assume you have only one network card. If you have "
"two, pick one and leave the other attached to ``sys-net``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:30
#: ab105ad0dec540a7ae0c67dca1bf584e
msgid "Remove the network card (PCI device) from ``sys-net``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:32
#: 90263eaaf01c444b84f2f5f76fd55a31
msgid "Restart your computer (for the removal to take effect)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:34
#: a31011dec4fb4833913ac64472407c4a
msgid ""
"Install ``dhcp-client`` and ``openssh-server`` on your testbench’s dom0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:36
#: 6e6d6fa53507428981b7a3f24d28e728
msgid ""
"Save the following script in ``/home/user/bin/dom0_network.sh`` and make it "
"executable. It should enable your network card in dom0. *Be sure to adjust "
"the script’s variables to suit your needs.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:77
#: a7d70240ef4546f2948f9fce749542db
msgid ""
"Configure your DHCP server so your testbench gets static IP and connect your "
"machine to your local network. You should ensure that your testbench can "
"reach the Internet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:79
#: c9581d583df9400299d1d8b8b79c4f89
msgid ""
"You’ll need to run the above script on every startup. To automate this save "
"the following systemd service ``/etc/systemd/system/dom0-network-direct."
"service``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:95
#: 3a4c10d64e994a15beadc1f5e13596fb
msgid "Then, enable and start the SSH Server and the script on boot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:108
#: 45e408a69ff9479e85bcd98a3f4fa5b8
msgid ""
"**Note:** If you want to install additional software in dom0 and your only "
"network card was assigned to dom0, then *instead* of the usual ``sudo qubes-"
"dom0-update <PACKAGE>`` now you run ``sudo dnf --setopt=reposdir=/etc/yum."
"repos.d install <PACKAGE>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:111
#: 3d666ba29a37422baf89efa663ae3061
msgid "Install Tests and Their Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:114
#: 96ccff6c6d614c9eafb11615b182230a
msgid ""
"A regular Qubes installation isn’t ready to run the full suite of tests. For "
"example, in order to run the `Split GPG tests <https://github.com/QubesOS/"
"qubes-app-linux-split-gpg/blob/4bc201bb70c011119eed19df25dc5b46120d04ed/"
"tests/splitgpg/tests.py>`__ you need to have the ``qubes-gpg-split-tests`` "
"package installed in your app qubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/test-bench.rst:116
#: 6034abb53cf04985ae6b4a536f6f58ea
msgid ""
"Because of the above reason, some additional configurations need to be done "
"to your testing environment. This can be done in an automated manner with "
"the help of the :doc:`Salt </user/advanced-topics/salt>` configuration that "
"provisions the :doc:`automated testing environment </developer/debugging/"
"automated-tests>`."
msgstr ""

